Z||000000||sqoach||06-30-2001||09:45 PM||||What's wrong? It seemed to be working ok before I changed the oil. Was a bit jumpy at times, but worked for the most part. Is there a sensor for this?<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">     <BR>84 SE (FOR SALE)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)(take it off my hands for $50)<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE sometime in this summer)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||06-30-2001||10:32 PM||||The oil pressure sensor for the guage is located:<P>4cyl-rear of engine, center of engine block<BR>6cyl-lower rh frt of engine<P>is a tan colored wire.<P>hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tryxalon||06-30-2001||10:35 PM||||Had the same problem. For me, it was a bad connection on the sensor wire. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||07-01-2001||01:34 AM||||Hey Sqoach!<BR>When you changed your oil, did you change brands or viscosity?<BR>Some brands are thicker than others, while a heavier oil increases pressure...<BR>I doubt it is a filter problem, if it were, it would read less, usually...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
